{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790971687,"nonce":"txOlxBJOgAVQWAooXzqErKRSwFk=","title":"Hot reload: nested component state, structural template edits, a frame hook","message":"HotReload (ashui.ui.HotReload) works for body-only edits on Ash: run with ash --hot-reload (hybrid or jit; interp ignores the flag) and call HotReload.check() each frame. When the .hl changes, every root component (one no other component's render built) renders again from the new code, its new root swapped into the old one's place, and keeps its fields, @:state included. Fixture: tests/fixtures/hotreload (sh run.sh v2: before 'v1 count=5 width=50', after 'v2 count=5 width=100').\n\nOpen:\n- Components built by a root's render are built afresh, so their own @:state starts over. Keeping it needs matching old to new instances, e.g. by component class and position under the parent, and handing the old instance's fields over.\n- Adding a reactive expression, handler or other closure to a template is not a body-only change. Ash accepts it on its LLVM path and then crashes (ash 67bd802bd2600108fb10bf50d8ea52d395f4e6d6616bcedc01de1a50d3c8f9b1, sh tests/fixtures/hotreload/run.sh v3). Until Ash matches functions by identity, only edits inside existing expressions reload.\n- Nothing calls HotReload.check() yet. Once there is a frame loop (rendering, 5acb19b), call it there, guarded by a compile flag so release builds skip the per-frame file check.\n- A body-only edit of two lines recompiles 72-98 functions, a few seconds; an edit that shifts findexes recompiles the whole program.","files":null}]}